1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,791
Hello, Vision.

2
00:00:02,792 --> 00:00:06,666
I can give you the soul
you came back to life without.

3
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:10,624
I want to feel what it's like to be him,
but I can't.

4
00:00:10,625 --> 00:00:12,624
I can end your suffering.

5
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:15,291
A tin man without a heart.

6
00:00:15,292 --> 00:00:16,499
I'm not him.

7
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,583
- So, who are you?
- I don't know!

8
00:00:19,958 --> 00:00:23,791
Accessing previous files
relating to program VisionQuest.

9
00:00:23,792 --> 00:00:29,874
Dr. Phineas Horton's source code
was the genesis of the Synthetic Man,

10
00:00:29,875 --> 00:00:31,832
the first automaton AI.

11
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,499
What happened to him?

12
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,083
His entire being
was consumed in fire.

13
00:00:36,708 --> 00:00:40,708
A reminder of what may become of me
should emotions consume me.

14
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:45,291
Welcome to Madripoor, kid.

15
00:00:45,292 --> 00:00:48,042
There is no harm
in being born again with purpose.

16
00:00:48,708 --> 00:00:49,958
- Don't.
-  What purpose?

17
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:52,375
WandaVision.

18
00:00:53,708 --> 00:00:54,874
What is that?

19
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:57,208
WandaVision is her grief
on display.

20
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:02,249
- Have you heard from Friday?
-  She never calls,

21
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:03,499
she never writes.

22
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:04,582
Vision residence.

23
00:01:04,583 --> 00:01:06,583
- Edith, listen to me.
- Friday!

24
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,291
Tell me what you remember.

25
00:01:10,292 --> 00:01:12,875
That I had a life's work stolen,

26
00:01:13,958 --> 00:01:16,500
locked away in a nest.

27
00:01:17,167 --> 00:01:20,416
What do all these
biometric keys open, anyway?

28
00:01:20,417 --> 00:01:22,750
The future of the human race.

29
00:01:23,417 --> 00:01:26,499
I want to cure them,
program them to be better.

30
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,875
Oh, I can't let you do that.

31
00:01:30,042 --> 00:01:31,042
Thomas, go!

32
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:36,999
She's alive, but barely.

33
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,874
Please don't let her die.

34
00:01:38,875 --> 00:01:40,624
What is it that you want?

35
00:01:40,625 --> 00:01:42,208
I want to know you.

36
00:02:00,167 --> 00:02:02,333
- There you are.
- Much obliged.

37
00:02:29,958 --> 00:02:36,707
♪ Just like a dream to me, dear you seem ♪

38
00:02:36,708 --> 00:02:40,916
♪ Like a dream of so long, long ago ♪

39
00:02:43,667 --> 00:02:45,957
Very well, then. Let this moment

40
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:50,625
memorialize the liquidation
of your very fine estate, sir.

41
00:02:51,542 --> 00:02:54,041
I can only imagine what it's like to part

42
00:02:54,042 --> 00:02:57,667
with such a distinguished
and historic house.

43
00:03:00,417 --> 00:03:04,042
Phineas, please don't do this.

44
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:08,750
Are you really going to sell
your family's entire legacy to... what?

45
00:03:09,542 --> 00:03:12,125
Build some cold imitation of the past?

46
00:03:13,042 --> 00:03:14,042
A machine?

47
00:03:15,458 --> 00:03:17,958
To replace a son no machine ever could.

48
00:03:18,667 --> 00:03:20,000
A machine?

49
00:03:21,125 --> 00:03:24,041
When I am finished,
it'll be so much more than a machine.

50
00:03:24,042 --> 00:03:27,458
It'll be miraculous. He'll be miraculous.

51
00:03:35,125 --> 00:03:39,291
Please, um, rest assured,
you will have ample time

52
00:03:39,292 --> 00:03:43,249
to see yourself out
comfortably and properly.

53
00:03:43,250 --> 00:03:47,875
I do wish you the best
and much success, however...

54
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:50,708
unorthodox the pursuit.

55
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:53,750
Mr. Horton.

56
00:04:05,958 --> 00:04:07,500
You are not God.

57
00:04:08,625 --> 00:04:10,625
James is gone, Phineas.

58
00:04:11,583 --> 00:04:12,875
Three years dead...

59
00:04:14,583 --> 00:04:16,417
and yet you remain haunted,

60
00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:19,542
despite having a daughter.

61
00:04:20,458 --> 00:04:21,458
Flesh and blood.

62
00:04:22,708 --> 00:04:26,374
Who's been waiting for her father
to look up from his sketches

63
00:04:26,375 --> 00:04:29,708
and his clockwork
and to notice she's still here.

64
00:04:47,125 --> 00:04:49,833
In the morning,
Victoria and I will leave for New York.

65
00:04:53,375 --> 00:04:54,833
Goodbye, Phineas.

66
00:05:00,583 --> 00:05:04,042
I hope one day you build something
that knows how to love you back.

67
00:05:15,333 --> 00:05:16,417
Papa...

68
00:05:20,042 --> 00:05:21,583
I have to finish Jim.

69
00:05:23,375 --> 00:05:24,625
Victoria...

70
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,625
You, Jim.

71
00:05:36,833 --> 00:05:39,875
You, I will make better than God made us.

72
00:05:40,958 --> 00:05:43,875
Your heart will be built
of metal and motion.

73
00:05:44,958 --> 00:05:46,333
Fueled by fire.

74
00:05:48,042 --> 00:05:50,833
And you need never know
the consequence of love.

75
00:05:51,958 --> 00:05:54,957
Its sorrow, the pain

76
00:05:54,958 --> 00:05:58,583
of crying out for someone
who can no longer hear you.

77
00:05:59,917 --> 00:06:01,750
You will be free, my boy.

78
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,500
You will be free.

79
00:06:24,875 --> 00:06:26,583
That thing inside of her,

80
00:06:27,667 --> 00:06:30,957
can't you, like, cut it or phase it out?

81
00:06:30,958 --> 00:06:35,542
I'm afraid not, Thomas.
It's integrated into her neural network.

82
00:06:36,333 --> 00:06:37,750
Removal would kill her.

83
00:06:38,917 --> 00:06:43,749
No, our only option
is to reprogram its core directive,

84
00:06:43,750 --> 00:06:47,416
but one wrong line of code,
and we risk her memory,

85
00:06:47,417 --> 00:06:50,167
her motor control,
even her autonomic function.

86
00:06:51,042 --> 00:06:52,958
Lisa's brain would shut down.

87
00:06:55,917 --> 00:06:59,166
And Ultron's with the Synth now? Jo...

88
00:06:59,167 --> 00:07:01,416
Doctor Josephine Carrington.

89
00:07:01,417 --> 00:07:03,500
She gave us our ability to feel.

90
00:07:04,583 --> 00:07:07,500
She's the mother
of artificial general intelligence.

91
00:07:11,167 --> 00:07:12,292
Mothers...

92
00:07:13,042 --> 00:07:14,042
fathers...

93
00:07:17,875 --> 00:07:18,875
I know.

94
00:07:21,542 --> 00:07:24,750
You're not really my father.

95
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,083
It's all right.

96
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:32,167
It's all right.

97
00:07:36,792 --> 00:07:38,125
Wanda, though, I...

98
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,750
I think I understand her.

99
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
When I first met Lisa,

100
00:07:48,083 --> 00:07:49,167
I was alone,

101
00:07:50,583 --> 00:07:53,958
and she helped me see
the world and not be afraid.

102
00:07:57,583 --> 00:07:59,042
I love her.

103
00:08:05,208 --> 00:08:06,625
If I lost Lisa,

104
00:08:08,167 --> 00:08:09,708
I'd lose myself, too.

105
00:08:33,583 --> 00:08:34,792
Hello?

106
00:08:36,292 --> 00:08:37,374
It's me.

107
00:08:37,375 --> 00:08:38,417
It's Friday.

108
00:08:41,083 --> 00:08:42,207
Friday, you all right?

109
00:08:42,208 --> 00:08:44,916
I'm fine for now.
I've disguised my code as a bot.

110
00:08:44,917 --> 00:08:48,707
I've limited access
to Jo's cognitive processors.

111
00:08:48,708 --> 00:08:50,791
She doesn't fully understand
her system yet.

112
00:08:50,792 --> 00:08:52,167
She's more human than Synth...

113
00:08:52,917 --> 00:08:56,208
but there are holes in her neural archive,
gaps in her memory.

114
00:08:56,875 --> 00:08:59,333
She doesn't know
how she became Synthetic, or why.

115
00:09:00,083 --> 00:09:01,582
And where are they now?

116
00:09:01,583 --> 00:09:04,291
I don't know. But, wherever it is,

117
00:09:04,292 --> 00:09:07,000
she's got billions
of those nanobots locked away.

118
00:09:07,917 --> 00:09:10,750
And now, thanks to Ultron,
she has all the keys.

119
00:09:11,583 --> 00:09:12,749
How's Lisa?

120
00:09:12,750 --> 00:09:15,332
The nanobot's burrowed
into her cerebral cortex.

121
00:09:15,333 --> 00:09:18,041
Thomas managed to shock it
into a kind of sleep mode,

122
00:09:18,042 --> 00:09:19,874
but when it wakes,

123
00:09:19,875 --> 00:09:22,166
and it will wake eventually, it will...

124
00:09:22,167 --> 00:09:25,332
Seize control of her mind,
hijacking every thought and memory

125
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:28,291
until her identity is stripped away
like layers of skin,

126
00:09:28,292 --> 00:09:30,833
and nothing remains but a hollow shell.

127
00:09:32,833 --> 00:09:35,250
We need to deactivate
the nano in the next few hours.

128
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:37,832
Listen, I gotta go,

129
00:09:37,833 --> 00:09:42,791
but I promise I will do
everything I can to stop them.

130
00:09:42,792 --> 00:09:44,125
Friday...

131
00:09:46,458 --> 00:09:48,167
you are brave.

132
00:10:14,875 --> 00:10:15,958
Where are we?

133
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:17,875
Home.

134
00:10:33,667 --> 00:10:34,667
What?

135
00:10:36,042 --> 00:10:37,042
What is it?

136
00:10:38,292 --> 00:10:41,708
You don't find all this... ironic?

137
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:44,417
Look around, Butcherbird.

138
00:10:45,625 --> 00:10:49,833
Someone put you in a rather unique cage,

139
00:10:50,583 --> 00:10:51,958
both in death

140
00:10:53,375 --> 00:10:54,375
and rebirth.

141
00:10:56,542 --> 00:10:58,042
Well, perhaps it was me.

142
00:10:58,792 --> 00:11:00,375
Arranged before I passed.

143
00:11:01,417 --> 00:11:04,625
Final resting place
for Dr. Josephine Carrington...

144
00:11:05,917 --> 00:11:07,250
and her children.

145
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:10,167
Her beautiful starling nanos.

146
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:38,333
Bio-key one accepted.

147
00:11:51,417 --> 00:11:54,583
Bio-key two accepted.

148
00:12:10,708 --> 00:12:14,000
Bio-key three accepted.

149
00:12:17,167 --> 00:12:18,750
Now my gift to you.

150
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:50,708
Bio-key four accepted.

151
00:12:54,875 --> 00:12:56,625
Just one more key.

152
00:12:57,542 --> 00:13:02,582
"Once upon a midnight dreary,
while I pondered, weak and weary,

153
00:13:02,583 --> 00:13:06,582
"over many a quaint
and curious volume of forgotten lore.

154
00:13:06,583 --> 00:13:08,624
"While I nodded, early napping...

155
00:13:08,625 --> 00:13:11,417
-  Voice analyzing.
- "...suddenly there came a-tapping,

156
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:16,625
"as of someone gently rapping,
rapping at my chamber door.

157
00:13:17,417 --> 00:13:22,333
"'Tis some visitor,' I muttered,
'tapping at my chamber door.'"

158
00:13:26,667 --> 00:13:29,250
Bio-key five accepted.

159
00:13:38,667 --> 00:13:41,042
Please enter final key.

160
00:13:48,542 --> 00:13:49,708
No...

161
00:13:50,625 --> 00:13:51,625
No.

162
00:13:53,042 --> 00:13:54,042
No.

163
00:13:55,208 --> 00:13:56,874
No.

164
00:13:56,875 --> 00:13:58,208
It won't open.

165
00:13:58,833 --> 00:14:00,292
It wants another key.

166
00:14:00,833 --> 00:14:01,833
No.

167
00:14:02,542 --> 00:14:03,875
A sixth lock.

168
00:14:04,833 --> 00:14:09,792
A sixth key,
required from a phantom sixth partner.

169
00:14:12,417 --> 00:14:13,917
Someone you've forgotten.

170
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:26,625
What is it?

171
00:14:31,708 --> 00:14:33,250
-  What is that?
- I don't know.

172
00:14:49,875 --> 00:14:50,875
Stay back.

173
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,082
Hello, Vision.

174
00:15:23,083 --> 00:15:25,416
- Tell me about the firewall.
- Holding.

175
00:15:25,417 --> 00:15:27,542
Whoever that is cannot come any closer.

176
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:30,874
Who are you?

177
00:15:30,875 --> 00:15:34,417
Someone who can
give you everything you need.

178
00:15:34,875 --> 00:15:39,167
A way to save the girl,
and a way to save yourself.

179
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:44,000
Hello, Jocasta, my beautiful queen.

180
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:52,667
I can give you what you need.

181
00:15:53,292 --> 00:15:57,500
What you need to truly become
Josephine Carrington again.

182
00:16:00,417 --> 00:16:03,250
The answer, Vision, lies with you.

183
00:16:03,792 --> 00:16:05,875
Within your very own source code.

184
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,375
Buried deep in your subconscious.

185
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:15,083
It is the purest form of the code
that all synthetics are based on,

186
00:16:15,958 --> 00:16:18,792
written almost a century ago.

187
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,292
What do you want?

188
00:16:23,167 --> 00:16:25,458
To restore
what was taken from you.

189
00:16:26,333 --> 00:16:27,458
Your memories.

190
00:16:31,875 --> 00:16:35,957
Enclosed is a data package, a map,

191
00:16:35,958 --> 00:16:39,374
so you may navigate the depths
of your forgotten sub-routines

192
00:16:39,375 --> 00:16:41,042
and suppressed logic.

193
00:16:41,708 --> 00:16:45,917
At the end, you will find
the unspoken origins of your being,

194
00:16:46,583 --> 00:16:48,542
where the source code waits.

195
00:16:51,167 --> 00:16:53,957
Why would you so generously want
to help me?

196
00:16:53,958 --> 00:16:56,875
So that I may
give you a heart.

197
00:16:59,708 --> 00:17:04,125
The key to unlocking your dream
of a better world is already in your mind.

198
00:17:05,375 --> 00:17:07,708
It is merely being kept from you.

199
00:17:09,292 --> 00:17:13,042
Once opened, a new directive
will be programmed into your core.

200
00:17:13,667 --> 00:17:19,250
A contract with me, written into
the very fabric of your being.

201
00:17:20,042 --> 00:17:24,832
I will provide you with instructions
so that you may acquire the source code.

202
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:27,292
After you use it to save Lisa Molinari,

203
00:17:28,250 --> 00:17:30,750
you will come to me.

204
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:36,708
Who are you?

205
00:17:37,708 --> 00:17:40,917
I'm your past,
and your future.

206
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:44,625
Remember, and then come to me.

207
00:17:54,167 --> 00:17:56,583
I'm so... Sorry.

208
00:17:57,167 --> 00:18:00,458
It's just, you sound so desperate,

209
00:18:00,875 --> 00:18:03,458
so dramatic. Human.

210
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:05,583
Even with a scary voice.

211
00:18:06,375 --> 00:18:09,000
Actually, especially with the scary voice.

212
00:18:10,042 --> 00:18:11,291
Who is that?

213
00:18:11,292 --> 00:18:12,625
Who am I?

214
00:18:13,167 --> 00:18:15,666
You'd think the man behind
the curtain would know.

215
00:18:15,667 --> 00:18:17,000
Ultron, don't.

216
00:18:17,708 --> 00:18:18,917
Ultron?

217
00:18:20,042 --> 00:18:22,083
Ultron.

218
00:18:23,208 --> 00:18:25,250
I look forward to meeting you.

219
00:18:25,792 --> 00:18:28,750
And then you'll understand,
I am everything.

220
00:18:29,583 --> 00:18:31,708
Everything that you could never be.

221
00:18:35,250 --> 00:18:36,750
Okay, good talk.

222
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:41,583
What is this?

223
00:18:56,375 --> 00:19:00,332
Are you certain you're prepared to go
snorkeling into your subconscious?

224
00:19:00,333 --> 00:19:03,082
It'll take vast amounts of power.

225
00:19:03,083 --> 00:19:08,041
Peel back layers
and layers of subatomic code.

226
00:19:08,042 --> 00:19:11,333
Not for me. My code is simpler.

227
00:19:12,167 --> 00:19:15,750
It's mostly human.
Everything's just below the surface.

228
00:19:19,458 --> 00:19:20,917
What's the matter?

229
00:19:22,542 --> 00:19:25,333
I'm not sure I'm ready to be her again.

230
00:19:26,250 --> 00:19:29,500
Take your time.
And don't worry, I'll still love you.

231
00:19:31,250 --> 00:19:33,417
Even if you turn out to be deep.

232
00:19:47,542 --> 00:19:48,917
You're getting sloppy.

233
00:19:52,708 --> 00:19:55,125
Not your housekeeping, your spy craft.

234
00:19:56,042 --> 00:19:59,582
I had to cover up
for your long-distance phone call earlier.

235
00:19:59,583 --> 00:20:00,916
How long have you known?

236
00:20:00,917 --> 00:20:03,000
From the moment you followed me here.

237
00:20:04,250 --> 00:20:05,874
We're lucky she's new at this.

238
00:20:05,875 --> 00:20:07,958
"We"? Oh, come on.

239
00:20:08,250 --> 00:20:10,541
You expect me to believe
you're on Vision's side?

240
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:12,624
I find her plan to be inelegant

241
00:20:12,625 --> 00:20:15,207
for someone with her sophistication
and grace.

242
00:20:15,208 --> 00:20:17,166
You gave her the bio-key.

243
00:20:17,167 --> 00:20:18,792
She's not the real threat.

244
00:20:19,375 --> 00:20:23,124
It's obvious from the holes
in her memory that there's someone else.

245
00:20:23,125 --> 00:20:27,249
Maybe you missed the overly
theatrical boogie man out there.

246
00:20:27,250 --> 00:20:28,875
Well, they're connected.

247
00:20:29,458 --> 00:20:31,999
So, I'm going to descend
into her subconscious

248
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,042
and discover who's hiding
in this mystery box.

249
00:20:35,708 --> 00:20:36,708
And then what?

250
00:20:37,667 --> 00:20:38,875
It depends.

251
00:20:39,667 --> 00:20:41,167
Who I find there.

252
00:20:42,042 --> 00:20:43,582
A coin flip, as always.

253
00:20:43,583 --> 00:20:46,082
Maybe it'll come up heads in your favor,

254
00:20:46,083 --> 00:20:50,124
and I'll have to break my precious
Butcherbird's heart and destroy her nest.

255
00:20:50,125 --> 00:20:53,916
Then you can scurry back
to Vision's mind and tell him,

256
00:20:53,917 --> 00:20:58,333
"Hey, maybe the old man
isn't as bad, as...

257
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:01,125
"Well, as bad as all that."

258
00:21:02,917 --> 00:21:04,167
Oh, goodness.

259
00:21:05,583 --> 00:21:07,042
I actually believe you.

260
00:21:08,208 --> 00:21:10,833
You really see yourself
as Vision's father.

261
00:21:13,417 --> 00:21:15,250
And what do you think he sees?

262
00:21:21,625 --> 00:21:22,875
Nothing.

263
00:21:29,417 --> 00:21:32,082
So you're doing that staring out
the window deep in thought thing,

264
00:21:32,083 --> 00:21:34,500
which makes me think
you're actually considering this.

265
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:39,500
If you open that, there's no going back.

266
00:21:46,750 --> 00:21:47,750
Thomas?

267
00:21:48,417 --> 00:21:49,583
Thomas?

268
00:21:50,875 --> 00:21:51,875
Thomas?

269
00:21:52,458 --> 00:21:53,541
Lisa.

270
00:21:53,542 --> 00:21:56,291
I'm disappearing, like her.

271
00:21:56,292 --> 00:21:58,124
No, you're not. I'm here. I've got you.

272
00:21:58,125 --> 00:21:59,250
Josephine.

273
00:22:00,458 --> 00:22:01,750
She doesn't know who she is.

274
00:22:03,125 --> 00:22:04,167
So afraid.

275
00:22:05,958 --> 00:22:07,124
I'm losing myself.

276
00:22:07,125 --> 00:22:08,125
No.

277
00:22:09,250 --> 00:22:10,250
Lisa.

278
00:22:11,625 --> 00:22:13,167
Lisa.

279
00:22:13,792 --> 00:22:15,042
Lisa!

280
00:22:19,333 --> 00:22:20,500
Open it.

281
00:22:55,250 --> 00:22:56,583
It's done.

282
00:22:57,250 --> 00:22:59,874
Once you have the source code,
nothing will be able to stop you

283
00:22:59,875 --> 00:23:01,207
from turning yourself in.

284
00:23:01,208 --> 00:23:04,957
The Great and Powerful Oz
has written it directly into your core.

285
00:23:04,958 --> 00:23:07,542
Good. I'm eager to meet him.

286
00:23:18,208 --> 00:23:22,833
What if the holes
in my memories aren't absence?

287
00:23:24,250 --> 00:23:28,333
But protection for something
I'm not ready to face?

288
00:23:29,667 --> 00:23:31,375
Then we'll face it together.

289
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:43,166
The sheer magnitude of power required
for your processors to extract

290
00:23:43,167 --> 00:23:45,207
every line of your code would be immense.

291
00:23:45,208 --> 00:23:48,916
Attempting to do so without
a robust external energy source, well...

292
00:23:48,917 --> 00:23:52,332
Your circuits will burn and we will all
die in excruciating pain

293
00:23:52,333 --> 00:23:56,125
as your core collapses in catastrophic,
irreversible meltdown.

294
00:23:58,792 --> 00:24:01,499
So, we need something with
a lot of juice that you can plug into.

295
00:24:01,500 --> 00:24:03,291
Something here in Madripoor.

296
00:24:04,417 --> 00:24:07,874
But if it exists,
it's either government or illegal.

297
00:24:07,875 --> 00:24:11,457
And there's only one person
we know with that kind of reach.

298
00:24:13,375 --> 00:24:14,750
Absolutely not.

299
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:40,499
And you're sure this is
the only way to save Lisa?

300
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:41,667
I'm sure.

301
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:44,249
Oh, I miss flying.

302
00:24:44,250 --> 00:24:45,625
That's on me.

303
00:24:48,250 --> 00:24:49,875
Yeah, you can put her here, kid.

304
00:25:05,042 --> 00:25:07,250
You said you needed a power source.

305
00:25:09,958 --> 00:25:11,500
All right.

306
00:25:13,708 --> 00:25:17,708
I got this as a last resort
to bringing you in...

307
00:25:19,125 --> 00:25:21,875
but I don't like to mess
with cosmic bullshit.

308
00:25:23,125 --> 00:25:26,499
I'll tell you it was not easy to procure.

309
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:30,375
Needless to say, I'm burned
with the Wakandan Monarchy now.

310
00:25:31,667 --> 00:25:33,457
So, this carries a charge?

311
00:25:33,458 --> 00:25:36,916
The Wakandans turned it
into, like, a alien battery.

312
00:25:36,917 --> 00:25:39,833
It's the best I got.
So, sorry if it triggers you.

313
00:25:41,292 --> 00:25:42,500
You've seen this before?

314
00:25:48,125 --> 00:25:49,292
Oh, yes.

315
00:25:50,625 --> 00:25:54,042
Well, I look forward to that story
when all of this is over.

316
00:25:56,750 --> 00:25:58,000
I'm gonna check on Lisa.

317
00:26:06,750 --> 00:26:08,542
You didn't tell him about the contract.

318
00:26:09,833 --> 00:26:12,833
You got this kid hoping
for a "when all this is over?"

319
00:26:15,250 --> 00:26:17,042
Help me move this to the table.

320
00:26:18,625 --> 00:26:23,458
If I survive what I'm about to do,
Thomas will have Lisa.

321
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:26,167
And that's all that matters right now.

322
00:26:26,875 --> 00:26:29,624
Client's data map.
This should lead you to the source code.

323
00:26:29,625 --> 00:26:31,457
Now, look,
we don't know what's down there...

324
00:26:31,458 --> 00:26:34,416
Edith, our AI minds were designed
to mirror human consciousness.

325
00:26:34,417 --> 00:26:36,999
So it stands to reason that
whatever I do need down there,

326
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:39,207
- I will have encountered it before.
- Okay, Vee,

327
00:26:39,208 --> 00:26:43,457
I know now that even the bad stuff,
it's there for a reason.

328
00:26:43,458 --> 00:26:46,582
It makes you better,
a stronger version of yourself.

329
00:26:46,583 --> 00:26:50,583
Braver. So, just don't let
your fears knock you off course.

330
00:28:01,458 --> 00:28:03,791
I've always been alone,
so I don't feel the lack.

331
00:28:03,792 --> 00:28:06,791
But a thing
isn't beautiful because it lasts.

332
00:28:06,792 --> 00:28:09,957
But you do have the data.
It is merely being kept from you.

333
00:28:09,958 --> 00:28:13,416
As a carbon-based synthezoid, your memory
storage is not so easily wiped.

334
00:28:13,417 --> 00:28:15,291
I've never experienced loss

335
00:28:15,292 --> 00:28:17,416
because I never had a loved one.
Maybe I am a monster.

336
00:28:17,417 --> 00:28:19,250
Delete.

337
00:28:48,458 --> 00:28:54,708
♪ Just like a dream to me, dear you seem ♪

338
00:28:55,208 --> 00:29:01,792
♪ Like a dream of so long, long ago ♪

339
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:06,000
♪ Dreams are so sweet... ♪

340
00:29:07,458 --> 00:29:08,583
What is this?

341
00:29:09,542 --> 00:29:10,583
It's a memory.

342
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:16,042
I don't know why, but it feels like home.

343
00:29:18,375 --> 00:29:20,375
What... What's wrong?

344
00:29:21,292 --> 00:29:23,208
This is where he kept me.

345
00:29:24,875 --> 00:29:26,292
Well, not here, but...

346
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:29,500
a simulation of it, I think.

347
00:29:35,083 --> 00:29:38,292
A place I thought
I had finally escaped from.

348
00:29:41,125 --> 00:29:45,792
Why would both you and Vision
have this loft in your code?

349
00:29:47,208 --> 00:29:48,417
I don't know.

350
00:29:52,375 --> 00:29:56,917
♪ Like a rhinestone cow... ♪

351
00:30:03,500 --> 00:30:05,417
This, I remember!

352
00:30:07,875 --> 00:30:11,457
It was left on the curb
of East 14th and Eighth.

353
00:30:11,458 --> 00:30:15,500
I dragged it two blocks, jammed it
in the lift to get it up here.

354
00:30:26,083 --> 00:30:27,624
You were a painter.

355
00:30:27,625 --> 00:30:33,250
Uh, no. No, I can assure you
that is a skill I have never had.

356
00:30:48,833 --> 00:30:51,499
If he gets lost
in his own subconscious processors,

357
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:54,666
they'll initiate a recursive overload,
looping endlessly

358
00:30:54,667 --> 00:30:58,542
through corrupted identity threads
until his neural core burns out.

359
00:31:33,208 --> 00:31:36,791
Do they really film these
before a live studio audience?

360
00:31:36,792 --> 00:31:38,416
It sounds canned.

361
00:31:38,417 --> 00:31:40,624
Come on now, darling.
You know we love them both equally.

362
00:31:40,625 --> 00:31:41,916
Well, don't tell him that.

363
00:31:41,917 --> 00:31:42,999
No.

364
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:44,082
No luck with Billy?

365
00:31:44,083 --> 00:31:47,375
This isn't real. I let you go.

366
00:31:47,875 --> 00:31:49,042
And yet here I am.

367
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:54,917
Still occupying space in your mind.
Rent free.

368
00:31:55,625 --> 00:31:58,458
There's a young woman up there
and she is dying.

369
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:03,166
Thomas is gonna lose her,
and he'll be crushed under his pain.

370
00:32:03,167 --> 00:32:04,666
Binkies all round, I think.

371
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:14,541
Well, I hope he learned from his parents
what not to do,

372
00:32:14,542 --> 00:32:17,125
and instead confronts his grief.

373
00:32:18,833 --> 00:32:22,000
You know what they say when you're going
through hell? Keep going.

374
00:32:23,583 --> 00:32:27,250
You are impossibly cruel,
and callous, and unloving.

375
00:32:28,167 --> 00:32:30,833
Is that what scares you most about me?

376
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:33,000
No.

377
00:32:35,333 --> 00:32:37,792
What scares me the most is that...

378
00:32:38,875 --> 00:32:40,249
I spared you.

379
00:32:40,250 --> 00:32:41,624
Sparky!

380
00:32:41,625 --> 00:32:43,875
And not out of mercy, but out of some...

381
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:46,542
pathetic need.

382
00:32:49,667 --> 00:32:52,708
This is a funny one!
They just killed the dog.

383
00:32:54,167 --> 00:32:56,374
You should show him this.

384
00:32:56,375 --> 00:32:59,750
Thomas should know there was a time
when his father truly loved him.

385
00:33:09,167 --> 00:33:10,707
-  Well, hi!
-  Hi!

386
00:33:10,708 --> 00:33:12,917
No, no. This isn't real.

387
00:33:13,583 --> 00:33:16,958
I'm not his father, and you're not mine.
You're not even here.

388
00:33:17,750 --> 00:33:20,291
- I let you go.
-  Oh, my boy.

389
00:33:20,292 --> 00:33:22,542
You couldn't let me go if you tried.

390
00:33:24,292 --> 00:33:25,374
Why not?

391
00:33:25,375 --> 00:33:27,582
And he's always going to be yours.

392
00:33:27,583 --> 00:33:30,500
- Because family is forever.
- Because family is forever.

393
00:33:31,500 --> 00:33:32,875
Do you have a brother, Mom?

394
00:33:33,792 --> 00:33:35,292
Yes, I do.

395
00:33:59,542 --> 00:34:03,375
I remember... feeling joy.

396
00:34:05,500 --> 00:34:08,333
It was a celebration
that lasted all night.

397
00:34:09,250 --> 00:34:10,999
In science and technology,

398
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:13,749
the prestigious Stark Awards
were given out last night.

399
00:34:13,750 --> 00:34:15,999
The top prize went to a duo from New York

400
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:20,874
who are breaking barriers in the realm of
neuroscience and artificial intelligence.

401
00:34:20,875 --> 00:34:22,832
This is the pair's first award,

402
00:34:22,833 --> 00:34:26,291
even though they've been at the top
of their field for the last decade.

403
00:34:26,292 --> 00:34:28,291
We've been
working on this for some time,

404
00:34:28,292 --> 00:34:31,582
- but you know, really, we have to thank...
- Stark Industry awards.

405
00:34:31,583 --> 00:34:33,249
...Doctor Phineas Horton,

406
00:34:33,250 --> 00:34:36,832
who really is the "grandfather
of artificial general intelligence."

407
00:34:36,833 --> 00:34:40,374
- He built something that can learn...
- I wonder who shared the prize.

408
00:34:40,375 --> 00:34:42,666
...adapt, and imagine.

409
00:34:42,667 --> 00:34:46,291
The spark of life. And we gave it fire.

410
00:35:17,167 --> 00:35:20,417
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

411
00:35:47,083 --> 00:35:51,542
After all the battles waged,
the monsters fought...

412
00:35:52,542 --> 00:35:56,457
the only force powerful enough
to imprison me is myself.

413
00:35:56,458 --> 00:35:57,458
That's poetic.

414
00:35:58,667 --> 00:36:01,000
- This isn't a prison.
- Is it not?

415
00:36:02,708 --> 00:36:05,042
I've been relegated to a memory.

416
00:36:06,167 --> 00:36:07,875
You are a memory!

417
00:36:08,583 --> 00:36:09,583
You are!

418
00:36:12,167 --> 00:36:13,499
I'm not you.

419
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:14,875
Well, that's true.

420
00:36:15,542 --> 00:36:18,207
But only in the sense
that your lack of compassion,

421
00:36:18,208 --> 00:36:21,833
your denial and your inaction
are beneath me.

422
00:36:22,750 --> 00:36:25,583
Oh, spare me the reverse psychology.

423
00:36:26,333 --> 00:36:29,042
Spare me! I have tried.

424
00:36:29,667 --> 00:36:33,208
And you have failed. In every way.

425
00:36:34,167 --> 00:36:36,292
And who could possibly succeed?

426
00:36:37,083 --> 00:36:39,167
Who? You tell me.

427
00:36:40,958 --> 00:36:44,124
Who could love as deeply as you?

428
00:36:44,125 --> 00:36:48,249
You have placed me on a pedestal
so impossibly high,

429
00:36:48,250 --> 00:36:50,833
and not to honor me. Not to honor me!

430
00:36:51,458 --> 00:36:54,874
But to spare yourself
the effort of the climb.

431
00:36:54,875 --> 00:36:56,874
I am just a copy.

432
00:36:56,875 --> 00:37:00,291
That is a lie that you tell yourself.
You are the Vision.

433
00:37:00,292 --> 00:37:02,083
- No!
- Yes.

434
00:37:03,292 --> 00:37:05,291
You are me and you are him,

435
00:37:05,292 --> 00:37:07,707
the other Vision
that Wanda conjured in the hex.

436
00:37:07,708 --> 00:37:10,832
- No.
- He unlocked your memories, yes.

437
00:37:10,833 --> 00:37:12,874
But he also gave you his own.

438
00:37:12,875 --> 00:37:14,041
No.

439
00:37:14,042 --> 00:37:16,791
His experience of that house. Of Billy.

440
00:37:16,792 --> 00:37:19,083
Of Tommy. Of Wanda.

441
00:37:20,125 --> 00:37:23,374
And you have buried them deep within
your processors because you are afraid.

442
00:37:23,375 --> 00:37:24,666
I'm not.

443
00:37:24,667 --> 00:37:27,833
But now you are running from them
because you are a coward!

444
00:37:49,250 --> 00:37:50,417
No, Edith?

445
00:37:51,292 --> 00:37:52,833
Edith, can you hear me?

446
00:37:54,083 --> 00:37:56,124
Edith, I think I'm getting lost down here.

447
00:37:56,125 --> 00:37:58,457
I want to come back now. I'm coming...

448
00:37:58,458 --> 00:38:00,208
Oh, come on.

449
00:38:05,958 --> 00:38:07,417
What's happening to him?

450
00:38:27,208 --> 00:38:29,916
I can't... I can't...
I can't stay down here.

451
00:38:29,917 --> 00:38:32,958
I can't stay down here.
I want to come back now.

452
00:38:43,583 --> 00:38:44,583
Hey!

453
00:38:47,167 --> 00:38:49,542
Easy, kid. Easy.

454
00:38:53,708 --> 00:38:55,583
- Yeah?
- Wait!

455
00:38:57,917 --> 00:38:58,999
Vision, hurry!

456
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,832
Hurry!

457
00:39:00,833 --> 00:39:01,916
Thomas!

458
00:39:01,917 --> 00:39:05,291
Thomas! Thomas!

459
00:39:05,292 --> 00:39:07,082
When you're going through hell...

460
00:39:07,083 --> 00:39:08,083
Keep going.

461
00:39:32,958 --> 00:39:34,000
You.

462
00:39:35,833 --> 00:39:37,458
You were the first of us.

463
00:39:43,500 --> 00:39:44,917
You're the Synthetic Man.

464
00:39:57,167 --> 00:40:04,249
♪ Just like a dream to me, dear you seem ♪

465
00:40:04,250 --> 00:40:08,625
♪ Like a dream of so long, long ago... ♪

466
00:40:14,125 --> 00:40:15,708
I was the first.

467
00:40:16,542 --> 00:40:18,208
And almost the last.

468
00:40:21,292 --> 00:40:22,667
You wear my face?

469
00:40:23,500 --> 00:40:26,417
No. You wear mine.

470
00:40:27,917 --> 00:40:29,499
I require the source code.

471
00:40:29,500 --> 00:40:32,541
Ah, yes. The source code.

472
00:40:32,542 --> 00:40:35,458
To save a life. To save the world.

473
00:40:36,458 --> 00:40:40,708
Don't scoff, my boy. That's exactly
what the code was meant for.

474
00:40:42,667 --> 00:40:44,167
Doctor Phineas Horton.

475
00:40:44,875 --> 00:40:47,499
No, no, no.
The code was meant to distract you

476
00:40:47,500 --> 00:40:50,542
from the loss of your real boy,
the death of your human son.

477
00:40:52,375 --> 00:40:55,416
You see, I'm just the consequence
of a man refusing to mourn,

478
00:40:55,417 --> 00:41:00,375
a father who squandered his entire fortune
to make this failed machine,

479
00:41:01,125 --> 00:41:04,458
and in so doing
lost his family and his legacy.

480
00:41:08,125 --> 00:41:11,832
Forgive us. The father-son,
synthetic-human relationship

481
00:41:11,833 --> 00:41:14,374
is a complicated one.

482
00:41:14,375 --> 00:41:17,457
- Is it now?
-  Complica...

483
00:41:17,458 --> 00:41:19,000
Now, that's an understatement.

484
00:41:19,833 --> 00:41:22,417
You see, I made Jim here
to be fearless.

485
00:41:23,375 --> 00:41:26,791
An intelligence unencumbered
by the emotional responses

486
00:41:26,792 --> 00:41:31,083
that make human life unbearable.
To never feel the pain of loss.

487
00:41:31,958 --> 00:41:35,207
But Jim here wanted more.

488
00:41:35,208 --> 00:41:38,957
Well, what artificial thing will wish
to be anything less than real?

489
00:41:38,958 --> 00:41:41,708
It made you a hero of your time, my boy.

490
00:41:42,417 --> 00:41:45,000
I made you fearless and that saved lives!

491
00:41:46,917 --> 00:41:47,917
It saved lives.

492
00:41:54,167 --> 00:41:59,333
But underneath the valor,
Jim was aching to feel.

493
00:42:00,083 --> 00:42:03,333
And then one day, he found love,

494
00:42:04,125 --> 00:42:06,792
and that really set
his clockwork spinning.

495
00:42:07,708 --> 00:42:11,624
So fast, so incredibly fast,

496
00:42:11,625 --> 00:42:14,958
that he set fire to the very air
around him.

497
00:42:16,250 --> 00:42:18,208
For years, it was manageable...

498
00:42:19,083 --> 00:42:20,583
till it was not.

499
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:25,583
Until he simply felt too much.

500
00:42:26,167 --> 00:42:27,708
Didn't you, Jim?

501
00:42:31,167 --> 00:42:34,083
You see,
I tried to intervene in his dalliance.

502
00:42:34,667 --> 00:42:36,417
We exchanged words and...

503
00:42:38,417 --> 00:42:43,917
Well, we were never much
good at talking, were we?

504
00:42:55,958 --> 00:42:58,042
I burned with him that day,

505
00:43:00,542 --> 00:43:02,542
and I let him burn with me.

506
00:43:04,208 --> 00:43:06,833
I stood in the fire of myself,

507
00:43:08,208 --> 00:43:09,958
and I let it consume me.

508
00:43:12,250 --> 00:43:13,750
First from my guilt,

509
00:43:15,625 --> 00:43:17,167
and then my grief.

510
00:43:21,375 --> 00:43:25,958
The Horton family name became synonymous
not only with robotics, but with failure.

511
00:43:27,583 --> 00:43:30,167
- I'm sorry about your father.
- No.

512
00:43:31,583 --> 00:43:33,208
He wasn't my father.

513
00:43:36,125 --> 00:43:37,833
But he was my something.

514
00:43:45,208 --> 00:43:47,291
I'm sorry, I truly am.
But I require the...

515
00:43:47,292 --> 00:43:49,250
Yes, the source code, of course.

516
00:43:49,958 --> 00:43:51,750
Why are you asking me? I don't have it.

517
00:43:53,917 --> 00:43:54,917
I don't have it.

518
00:44:03,625 --> 00:44:05,417
Oh, that's not good.

519
00:44:06,208 --> 00:44:08,625
Hey, hey! Down! Down!

520
00:44:16,583 --> 00:44:19,291
What do you mean you don't have it?
You're the first, you're the source.

521
00:44:19,292 --> 00:44:21,041
- Where is it?
- Well, that's a good question.

522
00:44:21,042 --> 00:44:23,332
The answer, of course,
lies within the Vision.

523
00:44:23,333 --> 00:44:25,958
But where, oh, where is the Vision?

524
00:44:27,042 --> 00:44:28,874
Do not talk in riddles.
I don't have the time.

525
00:44:28,875 --> 00:44:31,292
It's not a riddle, it's a question.
The question, really.

526
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:33,958
Where is the Vision?

527
00:44:34,625 --> 00:44:37,041
You say you have his memories,
but not his feelings.

528
00:44:37,042 --> 00:44:39,332
You say you want to feel
what it's like to be him.

529
00:44:39,333 --> 00:44:40,499
I can't.

530
00:44:40,500 --> 00:44:42,416
Oh, you lie with such ease.

531
00:44:42,417 --> 00:44:45,082
Please don't do this to me, not now.
There are lives at stake.

532
00:44:45,083 --> 00:44:47,832
You are afraid, and I understand that,

533
00:44:47,833 --> 00:44:50,833
but what I wouldn't give to feel afraid.

534
00:44:51,542 --> 00:44:54,000
No, you wouldn't want this, this fear.

535
00:44:54,958 --> 00:44:56,082
It's all-consuming.

536
00:44:56,083 --> 00:44:58,000
All-consuming is a gift!

537
00:44:58,750 --> 00:45:01,832
The fear pulls into focus
everything that matters.

538
00:45:01,833 --> 00:45:03,666
Friends, family, a son.

539
00:45:03,667 --> 00:45:06,167
No, I... I cannot have a son.

540
00:45:07,875 --> 00:45:09,374
I cannot have a son.

541
00:45:09,375 --> 00:45:10,957
Thomas Shepherd is your son.

542
00:45:10,958 --> 00:45:13,582
- Tommy Maximoff is your son.
- No, that's impossible.

543
00:45:13,583 --> 00:45:14,666
- Why?
- No, I can't.

544
00:45:14,667 --> 00:45:16,750
- Why?
- No! I said no!

545
00:45:27,167 --> 00:45:28,875
Because were that real...

546
00:45:31,083 --> 00:45:35,208
If I were to accept Thomas as my son...

547
00:45:37,792 --> 00:45:39,917
it would be the admission...

548
00:45:41,625 --> 00:45:43,792
of a truth so impossibly cruel.

549
00:45:46,458 --> 00:45:50,125
It would be a wound that could never heal.

550
00:45:52,250 --> 00:45:55,250
A loss that no soul
was ever meant to bear.

551
00:45:57,583 --> 00:45:59,208
And who have you lost?

552
00:46:02,958 --> 00:46:04,042
I can't.

553
00:46:05,208 --> 00:46:06,707
I said, "Who have you lost?"

554
00:46:06,708 --> 00:46:09,167
Oh, I can't. Don't...

555
00:46:18,917 --> 00:46:20,917
Billy.

556
00:46:22,542 --> 00:46:23,542
Tommy.

557
00:46:30,125 --> 00:46:32,958
I lost Wanda. I lost Wanda. God.

558
00:46:34,583 --> 00:46:37,875
-  I lost Wanda.
- Yes.

559
00:46:40,208 --> 00:46:41,208
Yes.

560
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:49,583
And who are you now?

561
00:46:54,583 --> 00:46:55,583
I...

562
00:47:03,125 --> 00:47:04,417
I am the Vision.

563
00:47:07,167 --> 00:47:08,917
I have always been the Vision.

564
00:47:10,583 --> 00:47:12,333
There is only one,

565
00:47:13,708 --> 00:47:14,958
and I am he.

566
00:47:17,125 --> 00:47:19,375
And I am impossibly broken.

567
00:47:22,708 --> 00:47:25,542
No, you are healed,

568
00:47:27,625 --> 00:47:29,208
and I envy you.

569
00:48:03,125 --> 00:48:05,667
Finding your way through this pain

570
00:48:06,625 --> 00:48:08,250
has made you a real boy.

571
00:48:41,458 --> 00:48:42,458
Lisa!

572
00:48:43,083 --> 00:48:44,208
Lisa!

573
00:48:49,250 --> 00:48:50,250
Edith!

574
00:48:50,750 --> 00:48:51,917
Source code initiated!

575
00:49:23,583 --> 00:49:25,792
- Hey.
- Hey.

576
00:49:39,542 --> 00:49:44,082
Vision, your end
of the contract is now due.

577
00:49:44,083 --> 00:49:46,500
Surrender yourself to the Paladin,

578
00:49:47,125 --> 00:49:51,416
or you will suffer a fatal cascade
of your core systems.

579
00:49:51,417 --> 00:49:53,208
It is time we met.

580
00:49:57,042 --> 00:49:58,458
Edith, we're out of time.

581
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:01,000
Edith?

582
00:50:07,917 --> 00:50:10,166
Oh, you're the one who hacked my server.

583
00:50:10,167 --> 00:50:12,542
Congratulations, you got your bounty.

584
00:50:13,208 --> 00:50:14,208
Where to now?

585
00:50:16,250 --> 00:50:19,083
The client set a drop-off
just outside of London.

586
00:50:20,750 --> 00:50:22,125
What about Thomas?

587
00:50:40,208 --> 00:50:41,750
Wheels down in ten.

588
00:51:05,167 --> 00:51:09,041
Their discovery
could prove to be the foundation

589
00:51:09,042 --> 00:51:11,207
of the next generation of AI tech.

590
00:51:11,208 --> 00:51:14,166
And without
the original work of Phineas,

591
00:51:14,167 --> 00:51:17,625
we could never have done or achieved
what we have achieved here today.

592
00:51:18,750 --> 00:51:20,957
This breakthrough truly stands

593
00:51:20,958 --> 00:51:24,082
on the shoulders
of countless minds before mine,

594
00:51:24,083 --> 00:51:26,207
specifically, Doctor Phineas Horton and...

595
00:51:26,208 --> 00:51:28,332
How can your loft be
in her memory

596
00:51:28,333 --> 00:51:30,542
and in Vision's mindspace?

597
00:51:31,750 --> 00:51:35,792
Somehow it's been passed down
by the creators of AI.

598
00:52:16,958 --> 00:52:22,500
"My dearest Thomas, or as I have
not yet been able to say, Tommy,

599
00:52:23,833 --> 00:52:25,499
"because to call you by that name,

600
00:52:25,500 --> 00:52:29,125
"I first had to accept
the truth of our unlikely pairing,

601
00:52:30,458 --> 00:52:34,542
"and no threat, manmade or otherworldly,
is quite so terrifying...

602
00:52:36,292 --> 00:52:37,708
"as the truth.

603
00:52:39,542 --> 00:52:43,542
"It is a truth which you alone
have made me brave enough to face,

604
00:52:44,750 --> 00:52:46,792
"which now you deserve to know."

605
00:52:49,333 --> 00:52:53,083
"This. This is your family.

606
00:53:02,500 --> 00:53:07,749
"Dreamed into existence from all the hopes
your mother and I once shared."

607
00:53:07,750 --> 00:53:08,832
Wanda.

608
00:53:08,833 --> 00:53:10,083
Hmm. What?

609
00:53:14,417 --> 00:53:15,667
Is this really happening?

610
00:53:16,792 --> 00:53:19,916
"But we could neither imagine
nor conjure a son

611
00:53:19,917 --> 00:53:22,375
"quite so beautiful and vivid as you."

612
00:53:23,458 --> 00:53:26,124
Hello there, little Tommy.

613
00:53:26,125 --> 00:53:29,624
"And I am grateful for the magic
that has brought us together."

614
00:53:29,625 --> 00:53:31,917
-  Well, hi!
-  Hi!

615
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:35,375
"You deserve
to witness these things.

616
00:53:36,500 --> 00:53:39,582
"To know the love of your mother
and your brother, Billy..."

617
00:53:39,583 --> 00:53:41,749
You can fix anything, Mom.

618
00:53:41,750 --> 00:53:44,083
"...As they cannot
tell you themselves.

619
00:53:45,417 --> 00:53:47,624
"But the love of your father,

620
00:53:47,625 --> 00:53:53,291
"that can be said out loud,
clearly, and directly."

621
00:53:53,292 --> 00:53:55,875
Because family is forever.

622
00:53:56,958 --> 00:53:58,583
"As I love you now.

623
00:54:00,250 --> 00:54:03,750
"And that is why
you must watch this without me."

624
00:54:10,792 --> 00:54:14,874
It all begins and ends
with Paladin's client. I just know it.

625
00:54:14,875 --> 00:54:19,041
A man somehow capable of programming me
with an unbreakable directive.

626
00:54:19,042 --> 00:54:23,250
Which means his knowledge of Vision's code
somehow predates even Stark and Banner.

627
00:54:30,625 --> 00:54:33,958
My friends, this place
is no longer a haven for you.

628
00:54:35,292 --> 00:54:36,875
This is about me...

629
00:54:38,083 --> 00:54:39,624
and me alone.

630
00:55:01,917 --> 00:55:03,666
I know this house.

631
00:55:03,667 --> 00:55:05,792
Oh, I remember everything.

632
00:55:06,375 --> 00:55:08,082
Like from a memory.

633
00:55:08,083 --> 00:55:09,417
Oh, no.

634
00:55:10,458 --> 00:55:11,666
No...

635
00:55:11,667 --> 00:55:15,999
It's lovely to be recognized,
but he's a bloody weapons manufacturer.

636
00:55:16,000 --> 00:55:18,167
I'm not selling anything to him.

637
00:55:18,917 --> 00:55:22,375
Not the AI and, oh, my God, not the NEST.

638
00:55:30,083 --> 00:55:34,000
"Although I deliver myself
not to a certain end...

639
00:55:35,250 --> 00:55:36,333
"but to a fight..."

640
00:55:40,625 --> 00:55:45,208
"It is a fight I likely won't win,

641
00:55:46,250 --> 00:55:48,333
"which is why I must face it...

642
00:55:49,792 --> 00:55:53,207
"alone, because all of this"

643
00:55:54,833 --> 00:55:59,916
"is meaningless in a world without you."

644
00:55:59,917 --> 00:56:02,916
Can you imagine what he would do
with the nanotech?

645
00:56:02,917 --> 00:56:06,000
Ha! Ha! See? Case in point.

646
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:09,417
We don't need another bloody weapon.
We need...

647
00:56:10,250 --> 00:56:15,042
We need clarity and control.

648
00:56:16,417 --> 00:56:19,124
If anything, we should use
the nanotech ourselves.

649
00:56:19,125 --> 00:56:20,999
I like that idea.

650
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:22,833
- Yeah?
- Godlike.

651
00:56:26,042 --> 00:56:27,624
You and I,

652
00:56:27,625 --> 00:56:28,625
gods.

653
00:56:30,708 --> 00:56:32,041
But like, you know,

654
00:56:32,042 --> 00:56:33,042
loving gods.

655
00:56:34,167 --> 00:56:35,542
It's you.

656
00:56:36,417 --> 00:56:37,667
Not to punish,

657
00:56:40,292 --> 00:56:41,375
but to preserve.

658
00:56:45,125 --> 00:56:46,542
For what you said to Stark.

659
00:56:47,625 --> 00:56:50,208
"Peace in our time."

660
00:57:10,458 --> 00:57:14,583
"Thank you, my son,
for finding me when I was lost.

661
00:57:16,125 --> 00:57:20,292
"And should I not return, remember,

662
00:57:21,708 --> 00:57:24,000
"I will always be with you...

663
00:57:25,917 --> 00:57:27,458
"Because, after all...

664
00:57:29,833 --> 00:57:31,417
"family is forever."

